{"name":"Cherry Wine","hex":"#b04556","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cherry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small fruit, usually red, black or yellow, with a smooth hard seed and a short hard stem.","Prunus subg. Cerasus, trees or shrubs that bear cherries."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing or having the taste of cherries.","Of a bright red color; cherry red."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cherry"},{"term":"wine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An alcoholic beverage made by fermenting grape juice, with an ABV ranging from 5.5–16%.","An alcoholic beverage made by fermenting other substances, producing a similar ABV."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To entertain (someone) with wine.","To drink wine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cherry Wine","blocks":[{"text":"\"Cherry Wine\" is a song by American rapper Nas, released in 2012 by Def Jam Recordings as the fourth single from his tenth studio album Life Is Good (2012). The single features vocals by singer Amy Winehouse and was nominated for Best Rap/Sung Collaboration at the 2013 Grammy Awards. It is the final single to feature vocals from Winehouse."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/67/Nas_Featuring_Amy_Winehouse_-_Cherry_Wine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry_Wine","wikidata":"Q3667226"},{"title":"Cherry Wine (Hozier song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Cherry Wine\" is a song recorded by Irish singer-songwriter Hozier for his eponymous debut studio album, Hozier (2014). The song was released on 12 February 2016 as the seventh and final single from the album, with proceeds from downloads benefitting anti-domestic violence charities. It is a folk and indie folk song written by Hozier, whose lyrics describe the trappings of an abusive relationship while simultaneously retaining fondness for his partner. The song received acclaim from music critics, who praised its lyrics and sound. Commercially, the song peaked at number 32 on the US Hot Rock & Alternative Songs chart. The accompanying music video premiered on Valentine's Day, and was directed by Dearbhla Walsh and stars Saoirse Ronan as a domestic violence victim."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a4/Cherry_Wine_%28Hozier_song%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry_Wine_(Hozier_song)","wikidata":"Q28135890"},{"title":"Fruit wine","blocks":[{"text":"Fruit wines are fermented alcoholic beverages made from a variety of base ingredients ; they may also have additional flavors taken from fruits, flowers, and herbs. This definition is sometimes broadened to include any alcoholic fermented beverage except beer. For historical reasons, cider and perry are also excluded from the definition of fruit wine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/%D5%86%D5%BC%D5%A1%D5%B6_%D5%A3%D5%AB%D5%B6%D5%AB.jpg/330px-%D5%86%D5%BC%D5%A1%D5%B6_%D5%A3%D5%AB%D5%B6%D5%AB.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fruit_wine","wikidata":"Q633625"},{"title":"Cherry","blocks":[{"text":"A cherry is the fruit of many plants of the genus Prunus, and is a fleshy drupe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Cherry_season_%2848216568227%29.jpg/330px-Cherry_season_%2848216568227%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry","wikidata":"Q196"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/How_I_LIve_Now_-_Saoirse_Ronan_-_9723136534.jpg/500px-How_I_LIve_Now_-_Saoirse_Ronan_-_9723136534.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.